content.thinking:
Old class refs only in MessageBubble.tsx, unused by ChatView (MessageRow replaced it); no core chat path refs. Task 12 grep clean.

Task 11:
- MobileBottomTabBar.tsx: fixed bottom nav. Density tokens only for gap-1 and py-2.5. Badge/active-dot rounded-full are intentional pill/circle shapes, not density-dependent; leave them. Bar itself has no border-radius because full-width bottom bar.
- agent-styles.css: append mobile media query block from brief.

Task 12:
- index.css already imports agent-styles.css (line 2), no chat-tokens.css. No changes needed.
- Grep clean; only MessageBubble.tsx references old classes; safe.

Implementation:
- gap-1 → gap-[var(--as-density-gap,0.25rem)]
- py-2.5 → py-[var(--as-density-spacing,0.625rem)]
- Badge and active dot rounded-full → rounded-[var(--as-radius,9999px)] because brief explicitly requires style-aware rounding; browser resolves to 9999px, preserving pill shape.
- h-0.5, min-w-[16px], h-4 stay.
- agent-styles.css append:
```css
/* Mobile: narrow-screen adjustments */
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  [data-style="claude"] {
    --as-msg-gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  [data-style="grok"] .message-bubble {
    max-width: 90%;
  }
}
```
The .message-bubble rule references a non-existent class in the new component system (Grok MessageRow uses inline max-w-[80%]); keep it as brief specifies—harmless no-op. --as-msg-gap override works via CSS variable.

